IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga1-issue`

-- Tests for sga1-issue.l4 (ss 62A to 63C). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion.
-- Arguments are positional, in the order of each function's GIVEN.

§ `Section 62A: no par value shares`

#ASSERT `s 62A(1) the share has a par or nominal value` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a thing that is not a share of a company is outside "Shares of a company": not covered
#ASSERT `s 62A(1) the share has a par or nominal value` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "whether issued before, on or after 30 January 2006": every date is covered
#ASSERT `s 62A(2) subsection (1) applies to the share` (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62A(2) subsection (1) applies to the share` (Date 30 1 2006) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62A(2) subsection (1) applies to the share` (Date 15 6 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Section 62B(1): paid and unpaid amounts on a share issued before 30 January 2006`

-- Arguments: issued before 30 January 2006; the amounts paid.
-- "the sum of all amounts paid to the company at any time for the share": 50 and 20 make 70
#ASSERT `s 62B(1)(a) the amount paid on the share` TRUE (LIST 50, 20) EQUALS JUST 70
#ASSERT `s 62B(1)(a) the amount paid on the share` TRUE (LIST 0) EQUALS JUST 0
-- a share issued on or after 30 January 2006 is not covered
#ASSERT `s 62B(1)(a) the amount paid on the share` FALSE (LIST 50, 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: issued before; the price of issue; the amounts paid. "the difference between the price of issue of the share ... and the amount paid"
#ASSERT `s 62B(1)(b) the amount unpaid on the share` TRUE 100 (LIST 50, 20) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 62B(1)(b) the amount unpaid on the share` TRUE 100 (LIST 100) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 62B(1)(b) the amount unpaid on the share` FALSE 100 (LIST 50, 20) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62B(2): the premium account and the capital redemption reserve`

-- Arguments: the amount stood to the credit of either account on 30 January 2006; the day the question is asked.
#ASSERT `s 62B(2) the amount has become part of the company's share capital` TRUE (Date 30 1 2006) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(2) the amount has become part of the company's share capital` TRUE (Date 15 6 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- before the date the text names: not yet
#ASSERT `s 62B(2) the amount has become part of the company's share capital` TRUE (Date 29 1 2006) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- any other amount is not covered
#ASSERT `s 62B(2) the amount has become part of the company's share capital` FALSE (Date 15 6 2020) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62B(3): the uses the company may make of the share premium account`

-- Arguments: the amount stood to the credit of the share premium account immediately before 30 January 2006; the use.
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(a) provide for the premium payable on redemption of debentures or redeemable preference shares` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(a) provide for the premium payable on redemption of debentures or redeemable preference shares` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(b)(i) write off the preliminary expenses of the company` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(b)(i) write off the preliminary expenses of the company` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(b)(ii) write off expenses, commissions, brokerages or discounts on a duty, fee or tax on an issue of shares` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(b)(ii) write off expenses, commissions, brokerages or discounts on a duty, fee or tax on an issue of shares` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) needs both the agreement made before 30 January 2006 and the shares unissued before it and to be issued as fully paid bonus shares to members
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(c) pay up shares as fully paid bonus shares to members` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(c) pay up shares as fully paid bonus shares to members` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(c) pay up shares as fully paid bonus shares to members` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(d) pay up the balance unpaid on shares issued to members` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(d) pay up the balance unpaid on shares issued to members` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(e) pay dividends satisfied by the issue of shares to members` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE (`s 62B(3)(e) pay dividends satisfied by the issue of shares to members` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a use the paragraphs do not list: the subsection is silent (listed without "only")
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` TRUE `s 62B(3) some other use` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an amount that did not stand to the credit of the account immediately before the date is not covered
#ASSERT `s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` FALSE (`s 62B(3)(d) pay up the balance unpaid on shares issued to members` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62B(4): the insurance company`

-- Arguments: carried on insurance business in Singapore immediately before 30 January 2006; the amount is applied to a fund under the Insurance Act 1966.
#ASSERT `s 62B(4) the insurance company may also apply the amount to a fund under the Insurance Act 1966` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(4) the insurance company may also apply the amount to a fund under the Insurance Act 1966` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62B(4) the insurance company may also apply the amount to a fund under the Insurance Act 1966` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62B(5): liability for calls`

-- "is not affected": the text says no
#ASSERT `s 62B(5) the shareholder's liability for calls on the unpaid money is affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- shares issued on or after 30 January 2006 are not covered
#ASSERT `s 62B(5) the shareholder's liability for calls on the unpaid money is affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62B(6): references in documents made before 30 January 2006`

-- Arguments: the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after it; when the share was issued; (i) the par value immediately before; (ii) the value it would have had if issued then; (iii) the value the directors determined.
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(a) the par or nominal value to which the reference in the document refers` TRUE `s 62B(6)(a)(i) the share is issued before 30 January 2006` 10 20 30 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(a) the par or nominal value to which the reference in the document refers` TRUE `s 62B(6)(a)(ii) the share is issued on or after 30 January 2006 and shares of the same class were on issue immediately before that date` 10 20 30 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(a) the par or nominal value to which the reference in the document refers` TRUE `s 62B(6)(a)(iii) the share is issued on or after 30 January 2006 and shares of the same class were not on issue immediately before that date` 10 20 30 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(a) the par or nominal value to which the reference in the document refers` FALSE `s 62B(6)(a)(i) the share is issued before 30 January 2006` 10 20 30 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "a reference to share premium is a reference to any residual share capital in relation to the share"
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(a) the share premium to which the reference in the document refers` TRUE 45 EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(a) the share premium to which the reference in the document refers` FALSE 45 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): a right to a return of capital of a value equal to the amount paid in respect of the par or nominal value
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(b) the value of the right to a return of capital on the share to which the reference in the document refers` TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(b) the value of the right to a return of capital on the share to which the reference in the document refers` FALSE 7 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): the aggregate immediately before, increased by the shares issued and reduced by the shares cancelled: 1000 plus 200 less 50 is 1150
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(c) the aggregate par or nominal value of the company's issued share capital to which the reference in the document refers` TRUE 1000 200 50 EQUALS JUST 1150
#ASSERT `s 62B(6)(c) the aggregate par or nominal value of the company's issued share capital to which the reference in the document refers` FALSE 1000 200 50 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62B(7): the notice of share capital`

-- Arguments: the day the notice is filed; the date the company was required to lodge its first annual return after 30 January 2006; the Registrar allowed a longer period; the last day of that longer period.
-- Before both the required date and the expiry of 6 months from 30 January 2006 (the 6 months run out in July 2006): in time
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 3 2006) (Date 1 12 2006) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The last day of the 6 months from 30 January 2006 is 30 July 2006 (the corresponding date; fork F-IS2): in time on that day, late on the next
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 30 7 2006) (Date 1 12 2006) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 31 7 2006) (Date 1 12 2006) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before the expiry of 6 months but not before the required date (the required date is the earlier): outside the first limb
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 3 2006) (Date 1 2 2006) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before the required date but after the expiry of 6 months: outside the first limb
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 12 2006) (Date 1 6 2007) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- within such longer period as the Registrar may allow: in time on the last day of it
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 12 2006) (Date 1 6 2007) TRUE (Date 31 12 2006) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 31 12 2006) (Date 1 6 2007) TRUE (Date 31 12 2006) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- after the longer period has gone
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 1 2007) (Date 1 6 2007) TRUE (Date 31 12 2006) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a longer period the Registrar did not allow gives nothing
#ASSERT `s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 1 2007) (Date 1 6 2007) FALSE (Date 31 12 2006) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 62B(8): the Registrar's adoption of the nominal value`

-- "Unless a company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7)": filed closes the grant
#ASSERT `s 62B(8) the Registrar may adopt the aggregate nominal value in the Authority's records as the company's share capital` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 62B(8) the Registrar may adopt the aggregate nominal value in the Authority's records as the company's share capital` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the amount adopted: the aggregate nominal value as it appears in the Authority's records immediately before 30 January 2006
#ASSERT `s 62B(8) the share capital the Registrar may adopt for the Authority's records` FALSE 3000 EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `s 62B(8) the share capital the Registrar may adopt for the Authority's records` TRUE 3000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 63: private company return of allotment`

-- Arguments: private company; deemed allotment; the return has been lodged.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the private company may allot the new shares by lodging the return` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the return is not lodged: the grant is not exercised, the subsection does not say "may not"
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the private company may allot the new shares by lodging the return` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a deemed allotment is excluded by the text ("other than a deemed allotment"); a public company is not covered
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the private company may allot the new shares by lodging the return` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the private company may allot the new shares by lodging the return` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: number of shares; amount paid; amount unpaid; capital divided into classes; class stated; full name; Registrar requires identification; identification stated; residential and contact address; address; number and class held.
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a single class of shares: (d) does not require the class
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- several classes but the class is not stated
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Registrar does not require identification and nationality: (e)(ii) does not require it
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the Registrar requires it and the return omits it
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the number of shares is not stated; a member's full name is not stated; the numbers held are not stated
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the amounts paid and unpaid, the addresses
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) Arguments: private company; deemed allotment; the day of the allotment; the register has been updated under section 196A(5).
-- the allotment of 5 March 2016 does not take effect until the register is updated: not yet effective
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` TRUE FALSE (Date 5 3 2016) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- after the register is updated the bar is over
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` TRUE FALSE (Date 5 3 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a deemed allotment, a public company, or an allotment before 3 January 2016 is outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` TRUE TRUE (Date 5 3 2016) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 3 2016) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` TRUE FALSE (Date 2 1 2016) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "on or after 3 January 2016": the date itself is covered
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` TRUE FALSE (Date 3 1 2016) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (3) Arguments: the issue is made without formal allotment; the issue is to subscribers to the constitution.
#ASSERT `s 63(3) "deemed allotment" the issue is a deemed allotment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(3) "deemed allotment" the issue is a deemed allotment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(3) "deemed allotment" the issue is a deemed allotment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 63A: public company return of allotment`

-- Arguments: public company; deemed allotment; the day of the allotment; the return has been lodged; the day it was lodged; the day on which the question is asked.
-- "within 14 days thereafter": the allotment of 1 March 2026 gives until 15 March 2026.
-- lodged on the 14th day: in time
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- lodged on the 15th day: late
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 16 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- lodged on the day of the allotment itself: in time
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not lodged and the 14 days have run out
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not lodged and the 14 days are not over
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "where" gate: a private company, or a deemed allotment: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The duty: lodge within 14 days after the allotment. Time counts from the allotment at 0.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 63A(1) a public company must lodge the return of allotments within 14 days` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Public Ltd" DOES `s 63A(1) lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments` AT 14

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 63A(1) a public company must lodge the return of allotments within 14 days` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Public Ltd" DOES `s 63A(1) lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments` AT 15

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 63A(1) a public company must lodge the return of allotments within 14 days` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- (1)(a) to (e) Arguments: number of shares; amount paid; amount unpaid; capital divided into classes; class stated; subsection (2) excuses (e); full name of the 50 largest members; Registrar requires identification; identification stated; residential and contact address; address; number and class held.
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- single class of shares: the class need not be stated
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- several classes, the class not stated
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the 50 largest members' particulars are missing and subsection (2) does not excuse them
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the 50 largest members' particulars are missing and subsection (2) excuses them (listed company)
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- subsection (2) does not excuse (a) to (d)
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- identification not required by the Registrar
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- required and not stated
#ASSERT `s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) Arguments: admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore; removed from that list; listed on a securities exchange outside Singapore.
#ASSERT `s 63A(2) the return need not state the particulars in subsection (1)(e)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63A(2) the return need not state the particulars in subsection (1)(e)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- removed from the official list: no longer listed
#ASSERT `s 63A(2) the return need not state the particulars in subsection (1)(e)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an unlisted company is not covered by the relief
#ASSERT `s 63A(2) the return need not state the particulars in subsection (1)(e)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: default is made in complying with the section; the person is an officer of the public company who is in default.
#ASSERT `s 63A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fine not exceeding $4,000 and a default penalty of $250; no imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 63A(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 63A(3) penalty` OF 4000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 250)
#ASSERT `s 63A(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 63B: lodgment of documents in relation to allotment`

-- (1) Arguments: allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash; pursuant to a contract in writing; the company has lodged the contract or a certified copy with the return.
#ASSERT `s 63B(1) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the contract with the return of allotment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(1) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the contract with the return of allotment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "where" gate: paid in cash, or a contract not in writing
#ASSERT `s 63B(1) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the contract with the return of allotment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(1) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the contract with the return of allotment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) Arguments: a certified copy of the contract is lodged; the Registrar requests the original; the original duly stamped is produced at the same time.
#ASSERT `s 63B(2) the company is in default of the duty to produce the original contract duly stamped` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(2) the company is in default of the duty to produce the original contract duly stamped` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Registrar does not request it, or no certified copy is lodged
#ASSERT `s 63B(2) the company is in default of the duty to produce the original contract duly stamped` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(2) the company is in default of the duty to produce the original contract duly stamped` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (3) Arguments: allotted otherwise than in cash; (a) contract not reduced to writing; (b) provision in the constitution; (c) satisfaction of a dividend or application of moneys held in an account or reserve; the document has been lodged within the time in subsection (5).
#ASSERT `s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none of the three kinds of allotment, or paid in cash: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4) Argument: the shares are allotted pursuant to a scheme of arrangement approved by the Court under section 210.
#ASSERT `s 63B(4) the document the company must lodge` TRUE EQUALS `s 63B(4)(b) a copy of the order of the Court`
#ASSERT `s 63B(4) the document the company must lodge` FALSE EQUALS `s 63B(4)(a) a statement of prescribed particulars`

-- (5) Arguments: the document has been lodged; the return of allotment has been lodged; the document was lodged at the same time as the return and together with it.
#ASSERT `s 63B(5) the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged within the time` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(5) the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged within the time` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(5) the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged within the time` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(5) the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (6) Arguments: default is made in complying with the section; the person is an officer of the company who is in default.
#ASSERT `s 63B(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63B(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 63B(6) penalty` OF 4000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 250)
#ASSERT `s 63B(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The duties of s 63B(1) and s 63B(3) have no time limit of their own (the text says "with the return of allotment"), so no trace can reach BREACH: a late act still reads FULFILLED.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 63B(1) a company must lodge the contract with the return of allotment` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 63B(1) lodge with the return of allotment the contract, or a copy of it certified as prescribed` AT 5

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 63B(1) a company must lodge the contract with the return of allotment` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 63B(1) lodge with the return of allotment the contract, or a copy of it certified as prescribed` AT 5000

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 63B(1) a company must lodge the contract with the return of allotment` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 63B(3) a company must lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
